"rgba(0,0,0,0)", "widgets_values": ["{\"text\":\"控制时长60秒为一分钟\",\"fontSize\":50,\"fontFamily\":\"Impact\",\"fontColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#4d4d4d\",\"padding\":10,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"], "inputs": [], "flags": {"no_title": true}, "type": "PixaromaLabel", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(0,0,0,0)", "size": [524, 70], "pos": [1192.8297119140625, 1241.0328369140625], "id": 69, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfyui-pixaroma", "ver": "1.4.8", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PixaromaLabel"}, "order": 10}, {"showAdvanced": true, "outputs": [{"name": "CONDITIONING", "links": [65, 68], "label": "CONDITIONING", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "条件"}, {"name": "seconds", "links": [66], "label": "seconds", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "seconds"}], "color": "#233", "widgets_values": ["## Global Metadata\n\nA Mandarin Chinese-style pop song blending traditional Chinese instrumentation with modern cinematic pop production. Set the tempo around 86 BPM in 4/4, with a graceful, flowing pulse rather than a heavy groove. The overall mood should feel poetic, elegant, wistful, and slightly romantic, carrying the atmosphere of an ancient riverside town at night after rain.\n\nUse a pentatonic-inspired melodic language and spacious harmonic movement, but keep the topline accessible and memorable like a modern pop song. The production should feel refined and atmospheric rather than overly theatrical. Build gradually from an intimate opening into a broad, emotionally lifted Chorus, then resolve with a restrained and lingering Outro.\n\n## Vocal Details\n\nA young Mandarin female vocalist with a clear, soft, slightly breathy tone and an elegant lyrical quality. Keep the Verse intimate and controlled, with delicate phrasing and light ornamental turns inspired by traditional Chinese singing, but avoid sounding operatic.\n\nThe Pre-Chorus should introduce slightly longer sustained notes and a stronger emotional pull. In the Chorus, open the vocal tone and increase the melodic range while maintaining smooth diction and graceful phrasing.\n\nAdd subtle backing harmonies only in the later half of the Chorus. Avoid dense vocal stacking. The emotional delivery should feel restrained on the surface but quietly intense underneath.\n\n## Arrangement\n\nBegin with a sparse Intro featuring guzheng plucks, distant xiao flute, soft ambient texture, and a very light cinematic pad. Let the Verse enter with minimal percussion, warm low strings, guzheng accents, and occasional pipa responses.\n\nIn the Pre-Chorus, introduce a soft tom pulse, deeper string support, and a gentle rising erhu phrase to increase anticipation.\n\nOpen the Chorus with fuller cinematic drums, wider strings, stronger guzheng patterns, subtle pipa rhythm, warm bass, and expressive erhu counter-melodies. Keep traditional instruments clearly audible inside the modern pop arrangement rather than using them only as decorative effects.\n\nFor the Bridge, pull most percussion away and feature xiao flute and erhu around a more exposed lead vocal.\n\nReturn briefly to the final Chorus with the fullest emotional arrangement, then reduce everything for the Outro. End with a final vocal phrase over guzheng, xiao flute, and a soft unresolved-to-resolved string cadence, leaving a lingering night-rain atmosphere.", "[Intro]\n雪落旧长亭\n寒鸦掠过远山影\n[Verse]\n半盏残茶冷三更\n烛火瘦了灯芯\n渡口孤舟系缆绳\n像那年你背影\n枝头残梅落无声\n谁又叩响柴门\n我把归期写进星辰\n却照不到你归程\n[Pre-Chorus]\n若来世还能相认\n你是否仍等那扇门\n[Chorus]\n一场雪 覆了长安\n一炉香 燃到天晚\n我把牵挂折成了纸船\n漂过万重关山\n一场醉 醒在长安\n一声叹 隔了千山\n若你也曾回头看\n我还守在旧渡口边\n[Bridge]\n雁过留声\n人去留空\n只有长亭还记着我们\n[Final Chorus]\n一场雪 覆了长安\n一炉香 燃到天晚\n若此生还有一面\n愿与你再看江南\n[Outro]\n雪停了\n风还在渡口边", 222, "fixed", 60, 1.7, 50], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 64, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"widget": {"name": "caption"},